  "take": 180,
  "text": "In a match against a friend online, if your friend's phone loses its connection to the match for three minutes, or the game has waited five minutes for their move, you can now claim the win. The table shows how long you have been waiting and when you can claim, and you can always keep waiting instead. The server keeps the time, not your phone. Forfeiting while hands are still being kept or mulliganed now ends the game, online or on this phone; before, online, your friend was left at a table nobody could finish. Nothing you have saved changes."
